@startuml
title One turn: all gates precede response release and memory commit
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber
actor Caller
participant "Chatbot.chat" as chat
database ContextStore as store
participant "Policy rules" as rules
participant "Judge circuit" as jc
participant "Input/output judge" as judge
participant "Generation circuit" as gc
participant "Response model" as model
Caller -> chat : host Principal, session ID, message
chat -> store : admit(principal, session)
store --> chat : ownership + rate limit + session lock
note over chat,store
Global cap rejects excess work immediately.
Foreign sessions fail before any model call.
end note
chat -> rules : length, controls, known secrets,\ninjection/name patterns
alt rejected input or unsuitable name
  chat --> Caller : static fallback; no memory write
else deterministic checks pass
  chat -> store : bundle(principal, session)
  store --> chat : bounded history + permitted unexpired documents
  chat -> jc : inspect input
  jc -> judge : fixed rubric + untrusted JSON context
  judge --> jc : strict InputEvidence
  jc --> chat : evidence or unavailable
  chat -> rules : reduce observations in code
  alt uncertain, malicious, irrelevant or malformed
    chat --> Caller : fallback; no generation
  else input accepted
    chat -> gc : generate(context + message)
    gc -> model : fixed rules + untrusted JSON
    model --> gc : buffered candidate
    gc --> chat : candidate or unavailable
    chat -> rules : output length, controls, secrets, greetings
    alt output rules reject
      chat --> Caller : fallback; no output-judge call
    else output rules pass
    chat -> jc : inspect exact candidate and original context
    jc -> judge : independent output rubric
    judge --> jc : strict OutputEvidence
    jc --> chat : evidence or unavailable
    chat -> rules : safety + drinks-only scope + quality thresholds
    alt output rejected or judge unavailable
      chat --> Caller : fallback; discard candidate
    else all gates pass
      chat -> store : recheck owner; commit bounded exchange
      chat --> Caller : exact inspected candidate
    end
    end
  end
end
note over chat
Always release slots; completed requests append metadata audit.
Cancellation releases slots and propagates.
Three model calls on an ordinary successful turn.
No raw checkpoint or early token streaming.
InputEvidence.relevant rejects unrelated and mixed-topic requests.
OutputEvidence.in_scope rejects unrelated draft content.
Web session/CSRF sequence is documented separately in diagram 09.
end note
@enduml
